Tom: That sounds great. I really need some time in nature after a busy week.
Lucy: Me too. They say there are many rare birds in that forest.
Tom: Wonderful. Should we bring a camera to take some photos?
Lucy: Yes, but let''s be quiet so we don''t frighten the animals.
Tom: Good idea. And we must take all our rubbish home with us.
Lucy: Of course. We should leave the woods as clean as we find them.
Tom: Agreed. Let''s meet at the bus stop at eight in the morning.', 'Lucy 邀 Tom 周六去山里爬山;两人都想在忙碌一周后亲近自然;那片森林里据说有许多稀有鸟类;他们决定带相机拍照,但要保持安静以免惊扰动物;还要把垃圾带回家、让森林和来时一样干净;约定早上八点在公交站见面。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Lucy plan to do on Saturday?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Go hiking in the hills.","Visit a city museum.","Stay at home and rest.","Go shopping with Tom."]},{"q":"Why does Tom want to join her?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He wants to buy a new camera.","He needs some time in nature.","He has never seen the hills.","He wants to meet new people."]},{"q":"What does the forest have, according to Lucy?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Many rare birds.","A large car park.","A famous restaurant.","A small shopping centre."]},{"q":"Why do they decide to stay quiet?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["So they can hear the radio.","So they do not frighten the animals.","So they do not get lost.","So they can talk on the phone."]},{"q":"What will they do with their rubbish?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Leave it under a tree.","Burn it in the forest.","Take it all home with them.","Throw it into the river."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U1', 'sufe');
Mum: It''s lovely, Ben, but I''m not sure a wild bird should live in a cage.
Ben: But it might be safer with us. Outside, bigger animals could hunt it.
Mum: I understand, yet a wild bird belongs in its natural home, where it can fly freely.
Ben: So what should we do? It looks a little weak.
Mum: Let''s care for it until it is strong, and then set it free.
Ben: That sounds fair. I don''t want it to be unhappy in a small cage.
Mum: Good boy. Helping an animal back to nature is the kindest thing we can do.', 'Ben 在公园里捡到一只小鸟,想带回家养;妈妈觉得野鸟不该关在笼子里;Ben 说在外面会被大动物猎食,跟着他们更安全;妈妈理解,但认为野鸟属于能自由飞翔的自然家园;两人决定先把鸟养到强壮,再放它回归自然;Ben 也不想鸟在小笼子里不快乐;妈妈说帮助动物回归自然是最善良的事。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Ben want to do at first?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Keep the wild bird at home.","Sell the bird to a friend.","Leave the bird in the park.","Give the bird to a zoo."]},{"q":"Why is Mum unsure about the idea?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The bird is too noisy.","A wild bird should not live in a cage.","They have no room at home.","The bird costs too much to feed."]},{"q":"What reason does Ben give for keeping it?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It would be cheaper than buying one.","It can sing very beautifully.","It might be safer from bigger animals.","It is a very rare kind of bird."]},{"q":"What do they finally decide to do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Keep it in a cage for ever.","Take it to the city zoo.","Give it to a neighbour.","Care for it, then set it free."]},{"q":"What does Mum say is the kindest thing to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Help the animal back to nature.","Teach the bird to talk.","Keep the bird as a pet.","Take photos of the bird."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U1', 'sufe');
Anna: It''s beautiful here. Why was this reserve set up?
Guide: Years ago, this forest was almost destroyed, and many species nearly disappeared.
Anna: That''s sad. So what did people do to save it?
Guide: We stopped the hunting, cleaned the rivers, and planted thousands of young trees.
Anna: And did the animals come back?
Guide: Yes, slowly. Restoring nature takes many years, but the balance is returning.
Anna: What a wonderful job. I''d love to help with conservation one day.', '向导欢迎大家来到自然保护区,这里保护着许多稀有动植物;Anna 觉得很美,问保护区为何设立;向导说多年前这片森林几乎被毁,许多物种濒临消失;Anna 问人们如何拯救;向导说他们禁止狩猎、清理河流、种下成千上万棵小树;动物慢慢回来了;恢复自然需要很多年,但平衡正在回归;Anna 希望将来也能参与环境保护。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the reserve mainly do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Sell food to visitors.","Train animals for shows.","Protect rare plants and animals.","Build new roads in the forest."]},{"q":"Why was the reserve set up?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To make money from tourists.","Because the city needed more space.","To keep animals in cages.","Because the forest was almost destroyed."]},{"q":"What did people do to save the forest?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They stopped hunting and cleaned the rivers.","They cut down the old trees.","They moved all animals to a zoo.","They built houses in the woods."]},{"q":"What does the guide say about restoring nature?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It is quick and easy.","It takes many years.","It can never really work.","It needs no help from people."]},{"q":"What does Anna hope to do one day?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Open her own zoo.","Cut down the forest.","Help with conservation.","Sell rare animals."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required2', 'U1', 'sufe');

